frac{375\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}}{3}=125\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the side length of a single tank.\n\nSince the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{125}=5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $5\\,\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538940 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538940 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107285" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538940 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538940 #edb/ref 1071 "Six foam cubes has a combined volume of $162\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.$ Find the side length of a single cube." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538940 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "303cc00a-f8f7-5cb0-b148-e5fe2714f366" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538940 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the volume of one foam cube:\n\n$$\n\\frac{162\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}}{6}=27\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the side length of one foam cube.\n\nSince the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{27}=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $3\\,\\text{in}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538943 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186538818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538943 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107266" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538943 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538943 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ec/ec35ecf376e5f5108d379ee965b8ea7ce32223050fa09e8d90ad2cf769853894.png)\n\nThe volume of the cube above is $1\\,728\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$ What is the length of its sides?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538943 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3512c6b0-1995-511f-b3bb-e6f73ca555fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186538943 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as fol